<title>LUXEMBOURG: Italian farmers protest at EU.</title>
<headline>Italian farmers protest at EU.</headline>
<dateline>LUXEMBOURG 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Some 7,000 Italian farmers converged in protest on European Union farm ministers' meeting on Monday, wearing yellow caps, waving yellow flags and flying multi-coloured balloons.</p>
<p>The farmers demanded higher milk production quotas and a bigger share of EU subsidies for wine, olive oil and other Mediterranean farm products.</p>
<p>&quot;Farm prices are falling and farmers' revenues are declining. We want a fairer deal,&quot; declared Paolo Micolini, president of the Coldiretti farmers' union, one of Italy's largest.</p>
</text>
